      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({(\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}})}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{y}^{2}z+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(81-0) \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$",
